<Page
  title="Privacy · Octavo"
  description="What Octavo and this website send over the network, and what they never do."
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  heading="Privacy policy"
>
  <p class="lead">
    Octavo opens, edits and saves documents locally. Editing never uploads your files anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>What leaves your machine</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>AI features</strong>, only when you use them, and only to the AI provider whose key or
      endpoint you configured in Settings (or a local model server you run yourself). The request
      carries the text and context that feature needs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Web and image search</strong> from the AI panel, only when you use it, and only to the
      search provider you configured.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Update checks</strong>: shortly after launch and every four hours, Octavo downloads a
      small update feed file from its download server (Cloudflare R2). The request carries only
      what any download does (your IP address and the app's user agent), and installing an update
      always asks first.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What does not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No usage analytics.</strong> Octavo sends no usage statistics.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No account.</strong> Octavo has no sign-in and no cloud document store.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, and its fonts are served from the site itself.
    It is hosted on GitHub Pages, and installers and release information come from Cloudflare R2.
    Like any web server, they receive your IP address and browser user agent with each request.
  </p>

  <p class="updated">Last updated: October 21, 2026</p>
</Page>
